WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.500
Goal: understand why British cities apply 20 mph limits in residential areas, the passing distance when overtaking cyclists (at least 1.5 m at up to 30 mph) and the design of active travel.

2
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:30.500
Curriculum separation: the official DVSA test assesses the Highway Code and Hazard Perception. This complementary block introduces road planning and behaviour concepts inspired by transport studies such as the UCL Centre for Transport Studies (not endorsed by UCL).

3
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:43.800
Kinetic energy (E = ½ m v²): going from 20 mph to 30 mph raises the speed by 50%, but the impact energy is multiplied by 2.25.

4
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:51.000
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
